& [SelectedPurpose] is one pure supplied digest-pair reconciliation
  + consume exactly two completed WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest values by value
  + retain both complete non-deserializable digest carriers in one new output-only result
  + rederive both carriers from their retained plans and assemblies through the proven digest transform
  + require exact comparison profile, encoding profile, TopologyScanLimits, and root scope identity
  + report one closed equal or different disposition for the comparable canonical sequence commitments
  - never: accept raw plans, assemblies, members, observations, digest strings, or caller-declared equality
  - never: infer observation time, physical order, freshness, stability, quiescence, completeness, or receipt validity
  - never: construct TopologyReceipt or any admission object

& [WhyThisSlice] is dependency ordered
  + a complete output-only digest carrier already retains the plan, complete assembly, and exact ordered sequence commitment
  + pair comparison is unsafe when bare digests can bypass lineage, current validation, scope identity, or capability limits
  + comparison of distinct roots or distinct scan ceilings is a scope fault rather than ordinary inventory difference
  + equality and difference are both valid evidence outcomes once the operands are comparable
  + a pure pair result can later be consumed by separately authorized physical acquisition and receipt protocols
  + the pure layer must reserve temporal and quiescence vocabulary so later physical code cannot launder supplied equality

& [Input] is two completed digest carriers only
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest
  + [left] is one complete output-only operand
  + [right] is one complete output-only operand
  + both operands are consumed by value only after all pure checks succeed
  + each operand exposes immutable profile, encoding profile, plan, assembly, and ordered_inventory_sha256 getters
  + each nested assembly retains complete root, directory, regular-file, stability, content-binding, preflight, projection, and assembly lineage
  - never: derive Deserialize, Default, From raw values, public fields, or a public success constructor for either input or output
  - never: provide a bare-digest or raw-assembly overload

& [Plan] is strict and bounded
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliationPlan
  + [profile] exact cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest-reconciliation/0.1
  + [reconciliation_identity] is a nonzero unsigned 64-bit caller correlation value
  + [encoded_plan_maximum_bytes] is 4096 before strict JSON decoding
  + unknown, missing, malformed, overlong, wrong-profile, and zero-identity values reject
  - never: include digest strings, assemblies, roots, limits, timestamps, deadlines, expected disposition, physical claims, consistency class, receipt fields, or admission decisions in the plan

& [RoleVocabulary] is closed
  + [left] and [right] are supplied operand roles only
  + [comparable] means both complete operands pass current rederivation and exact common-scope gates
  + [equal] means both comparable lowercase ordered_inventory_sha256 values are byte equal under the exact common encoding profile
  + [different] means those two comparable digest values are not byte equal
  + [scope_fault] means the operands cannot truthfully represent one comparison subject because profile, limits, or root scope differs
  - never: name operands before and after
  - never: describe equal as stable, unchanged over time, double inventory, quiescent, snapshot equal, physically equal, or complete
  - never: describe different as malformed input when every comparability gate passes

& [CurrentRederivation] is mandatory on both sides
  + clone the retained digest plan and complete assembly from the left operand
  + invoke derive_windows_supplied_ordered_topology_inventory_digest on those cloned values
  + require the rederived complete left result to equal the supplied complete left carrier
  + repeat the same process independently for the right operand
  + preserve the exact nested left or right digest fault with an explicit side
  + stop before scope comparison or disposition if either rederivation fails or differs
  - never: compare only the supplied digest strings without current rederivation
  - never: duplicate, replace, or widen the canonical observation encoder

& [ProfileScope] is exact
  + each operand profile equals cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest/0.1
  + each operand encoding profile equals cantor-ordered-topology-observation-encoding/0.1
  + each retained digest plan repeats those same exact values
  + each retained assembly profile equals cantor-windows-supplied-topology-inventory-assembly/0.1
  + every profile mismatch is a scope fault or a side-qualified current-rederivation fault as appropriate
  - never: compare across digest, encoding, assembly, topology, or reconciliation profile versions

& [LimitScope] is exact
  + left assembly TopologyScanLimits equals right assembly TopologyScanLimits as a complete value
  + limits are comparison capability and coverage ceilings rather than sequence content
  + unequal limits reject as incomparable even if both ordered digest strings happen to match
  + assembly_identity, commitment_identity, and reconciliation_identity are correlation roles and do not need equality
  - never: silently choose minimum, maximum, union, intersection, default, or normalized limits
  - never: hash limits into the already signed ordered-observation digest grammar

& [RootScope] is exact identity, not full-root equality
  + each assembly has exactly one validated root-first member under the prerequisite authority
  + left and right root observations must have equal empty relative_path
  + left and right root kinds must both be Directory
  + left and right root strong identities require equal volume_serial and equal lowercase 32-hex file_id
  + root mode, attributes, link count, streams, length, content digest, and ordinal remain sequence content and may yield different rather than scope fault
  + root projection, entry-reference, preflight, stability, and carrier correlation identities remain retained provenance and do not define root scope
  - never: treat two different strong root identities as ordinary inventory drift
  - never: infer root path existence, physical identity freshness, handle continuity, or filesystem membership

& [Disposition] is one closed ordinary result
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliationDisposition
  + [variants] are Equal and Different with exact snake-case serialization equal and different
  + Equal is selected only by byte equality of both validated lowercase 64-hex ordered_inventory_sha256 strings
  + Different is selected only by byte inequality of those strings after all comparability gates pass
  + equality is qualified by the exact common encoding profile and ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions
  + no changed-field, path, member, byte, temporal, or causal explanation is invented
  - never: use bool because a named closed disposition preserves semantic role
  - never: treat Different as a transform fault

& [Output] is private, inspectable, and lineage retaining
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliation
  + derive Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, and Serialize only
  + private fields are profile, plan, left, right, common_scope, and disposition
  + immutable getters expose every complete field without enabling mutation
  + [common_scope] is a private Serialize-only record containing encoding_profile, limits, root relative_path, root kind, root volume_serial, and root file_id
  + the output owns each complete input exactly once
  + repeated equal inputs and plan produce byte-equivalent serialized results
  - never: expose public fields, Deserialize, Default, From, Into, a public constructor, a mutable getter, or partial success

& [Faults] are bounded, side qualified, and atomic
  + [codes] are json, profile, reconciliation_identity, left_digest, right_digest, scope_profile, limits, root_scope, resource, and internal
  + exact nested WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestFault is present only for left_digest or right_digest
  + [side] is absent except for left_digest or right_digest, where it is exactly left or right
  + field is at most 64 Unicode scalars and message is at most 256 Unicode scalars
  + no fault contains a digest string, complete operand, assembly, observation, carrier, common scope, or partial disposition
  + no partial success is returned

& [Ordering] is caller order without temporal meaning
  + left and right serialization order follows the function arguments
  + swapping unequal operands preserves Different but changes retained output serialization
  + swapping equal but lineage-distinct operands may change retained output serialization while preserving Equal
  + reconciliation never sorts, canonicalizes, or repairs operands
  + caller order is inspectable provenance only
  - never: infer acquisition order from argument position

& [EvidenceGrades] remain explicit
  + [supplied] all nested observations and content bytes at their original boundaries
  + [carrier_projected] complete output-only entry carriers
  + [structurally_assembled] bounded ordered supplied sets
  + [canonically_committed] exact supplied ordered observation sequences under the common encoding profile
  + [current_rederived] both digest carriers exactly reproduce through current pure authority
  + [scope_correlated] exact profiles, limits, and root identity are common
  + [pair_equal_or_different] only comparable supplied sequence commitments are reconciled
  + [physically_observed] absent
  + [temporally_ordered] absent
  + [stable] absent
  + [double_inventory] absent
  + [quiescent_double_inventory] absent
  + [receipted] absent
  + [admitted] absent

& [EffectBoundary] is zero
  + deterministic in-memory cloning, current pure rederivation, validation, comparison, and result construction only
  + no unsafe, Windows API, filesystem, path resolution, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, model, or tool call
  + no enumeration, traversal, Git reconciliation, physical fixture, physical double inventory, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, or promotion
  + no new Cargo dependency or lockfile delta

& [Requirements] are proposed
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-001] strict 4096-byte plan with exact reconciliation profile and nonzero identity
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-002] exactly two complete output-only digest-carrier inputs by value and no lower overload
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-003] independent current complete rederivation of left and right through the proven digest transform
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-004] exact digest, encoding, retained-plan, and assembly profile gates
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-005] exact complete TopologyScanLimits comparison
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-006] exact root relative-path, kind, volume-serial, and file-identity scope comparison
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-007] closed Equal or Different disposition over comparable digest values
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-008] private Serialize-only output retaining both complete operands and common scope
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-009] explicit caller-order retention with no temporal meaning
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-010] closed bounded side-qualified faults and atomic failure
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-011] reserved temporal, stability, double-inventory, quiescence, receipt, and admission vocabulary
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-012] zero effects, unsafe, platform calls, dependencies, and lockfile delta
  + [M2B-SOTIDR-013] focused, static, global, evidence, audit, rollback, and provenance proof

& [Verification] must be proportional and effect free
  + strict plan decoding covers valid, malformed, overlong, wrong-profile, unknown-field, and zero-identity cases
  + equal independently built assemblies produce Equal after complete current rederivation
  + one changed committed observation field produces Different rather than a fault
  + unequal entry count and member order produce Different
  + left and right nested current-rederivation failures remain side qualified
  + unequal digest profile, encoding profile, retained-plan profile, assembly profile, limits, root volume, and root file identity reject distinctly
  + correlation-only assembly, commitment, projection, and entry-reference identities do not decide equality when complete current carrier validity remains possible
  + swapped operands prove caller-order retention without temporal claims
  + serialization proves both complete operands and common scope are retained
  + static test rejects Deserialize, Default, public success fields, public constructor, raw input, bare digest, filesystem, platform, unsafe, clock, receipt, and effect surfaces
  + focused debug and overflow-checked release, workspace regression, format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, audit, and recursive evidence must pass
  + physical tests and effect-bearing builders remain uninvoked

& [Compatibility] is additive and strict
  + add one module and one lib export only after a valid future satisfaction signature
  + reuse current public digest transform and getters without modifying their semantics
  + do not modify the ordered observation encoding profile or known vectors
  + do not change Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, existing public types, existing tests, frozen evidence, or physical code
  + future physical code may consume this output only under separate source and signature

& [Rollback] is exact
  + remove only the future reconciliation module, export, tests, evidence, and closure records authorized by the future SJS signature
  + retain this raw source, manifest, SJS products, faults, and proof as immutable history
  + rollback never changes either prerequisite digest carrier or activates a temporal or receipt path

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  - stop before code until this exact source is processed through governing SJS
  - stop on any bare digest, raw assembly, duplicated encoder, profile coercion, limit normalization, cross-root comparison, boolean ambiguity, temporal naming, stability claim, inferred acquisition order, or partial result
  - stop on any claim that supplied equality proves physical repetition, completeness, unchanged state, atomicity, quiescence, Git agreement, receipt validity, or admission
  - stop on any effect, dependency growth, unsafe, platform call, or authority beyond this pure slice

